sion.\nElement `Account.procedure.device` has a context of Account based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `Account`.\nElement `Account.procedure.device` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>Account.relatedAccount (relatedAccount)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-Account.relatedAccount</td><td>Element `Account.relatedAccount` has a context of Account based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `Account`.\nElement `Account.relatedAccount` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>Account.relatedAccount.relationship (relationship)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-Account.relatedAccount:relationship</td><td>Element `Account.relatedAccount.relationship` is part of an existing definition because parent element `Account.relatedAccount` requires a cross-version extension.\nElement `Account.relatedAccount.relationship` has a context of Account based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `Account`.\nElement `Account.relatedAccount.relationship` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>Account.relatedAccount.account (account)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-Account.relatedAccount:account</td><td>Element `Account.relatedAccount.account` is part of an existing definition because parent element `Account.relatedAccount` requires a cross-version extension.\nElement `Account.relatedAccount.account` is mapped to FHIR R4 element `Account.partOf` as `SourceIsBroaderThanTarget`.</td></tr><tr><td>Account.currency (currency)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-Account.currency</td><td>Element `Account.currency` has a context of Account based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `Account`.\nElement `Account.currency` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>Account.balance (balance)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-Account.balance</td><td>Element `Account.balance` has a context of Account based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `Account`.\nElement `Account.balance` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>Account.balance.aggregate (aggregate)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-Account.balance:aggregate</td><td>Element `Account.balance.aggregate` is part of an existing definition because parent element `Account.balance` requires a cross-version extension.\nElement `Account.balance.aggregate` has a context of Account based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `Account`.\nElement `Account.balance.aggregate` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>Account.balance.term (term)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-Account.balance:term</td><td>Element `Account.balance.term` is part of an existing definition because parent element `Account.balance` requires a cross-version extension.\nElement `Account.balance.term` has a context of Account based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `Account`.\nElement `Account.balance.term` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>Account.balance.estimate (estimate)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-Account.balance:estimate</td><td>Element `Account.balance.estimate` is part of an existing definition because parent element `Account.balance` requires a cross-version extension.\nElement `Account.balance.estimate` has a context of Account based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `Account`.\nElement `Account.balance.estimate` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>Account.balance.amount (amount)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-Account.balance:amount</td><td>Element `Account.balance.amount` is part of an existing definition because parent element `Account.balance` requires a cross-version extension.\nElement `Account.balance.amount` has a context of Account based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `Account`.\nElement `Account.balance.amount` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>Account.calculatedAt (calculatedAt)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-Account.calculatedAt</td><td>Element `Account.calculatedAt` has a context of Account based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `Account`.\nElement `Account.calculatedAt` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).\nThe total(s) are not typically updated using the restful API but more often by back-end processes included in a typical finance system.</td></tr></table></div>"^^rdf:XMLLiteral ]
